      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "1. To find the inverse of $f$, where $f(x) = 3x - 8$, add 8 to both sides to solve for $x$: \n   \\[3x - 8 + 8 = 3x - 8 + 8\\]\n   \\[3x = 3x\\]\n\n2. Divide each side by 3 to express $x$ in terms of a new variable, $t$:\n   \\[\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)\\left(3x\\right) = x - 8\\]\n   \\[t = x\\]\n   Thus, the inverse function is $f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{1}{3}x + 8$.\n\n3. For $f(x) = f^{-1}(x)$ to hold, we set the original function $f(x)$ equal to the inverse function $f^{-1}(x)$:\n   \\[3x - 8 = \\frac{1}{3}x + 8\\]\n\n4. Combining like terms, we solve for $x$:\n   \\[\\left3x - \\frac{1}{3}x\\right] - 8 = 8\\]\n   \\[\\left(\\frac{9}{3}x - \\frac{1}{3}x\\right) - 8 = 8\\]\n   \\[\\frac{8}{3}x - 8 = 8\\]\n\n5. Moving 8 to the other side to isolate $x$:\n   \\[\\frac{8}{3}x = 16\\]\n\n6. Finally, multiply by $\\frac{3}{8}$ to solve for $x$:\n   \\[x = \\frac{3}{8}(16)\\]\n   \\[x = 6\\]\n\nSo, the requested solution is $\\boxed{6}$.",
